  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $x_1,x_2,\\ldots \\in (0,1)$ be an infinite sequence and let $ A_k=\\limsup_{n\\to \\infty}\\left\\lvert \\sum_{j\\leq n} e(kx_j)\\right\\rvert, $ where $e(x)=e^{2\\pi ix}$.\nIs it true that $ \\limsup_{k\\to \\infty} A_k=\\infty? $ Is it possible for $A_k=o(k)$?",
